# Map Poster Studio Development Rules & Invariants

## 🌐 Language & Interaction Rules (CRITICAL)

- **User Communication**: ALWAYS reply to the user in Traditional Chinese (Hong Kong / zh-HK) using professional local technology terminology.
- **Code & Content**: ALWAYS keep all source code, variable names, class identifiers, UI strings, file paths, and code comments strictly in English.

## 📘 Documentation & spec (read before you build)

**Authoritative sources (check in this order when the user asks for something new):**

1. **`.cursorrules`** (this file) — non-negotiable invariants, rendering contracts, API proxy rules, UI direction.
2. **`docs/adr/`** — architecture decision records (e.g. client-side Canvas rendering on Cloudflare Pages).
3. **`docs/design-direction.md`** — editor layout, visual tone, component composition.
4. **`README.md`** — stack, scripts, deployment, feature overview.

**Does every new feature require a doc update?** No. Update documentation only when **product or engineering decisions change** (new ADR-worthy choice, export preset, theme schema field, API proxy contract, or anything future agents must not guess). Bug fixes, refactors, and cosmetic UI tweaks that do not change behavior do **not** require spec edits unless they fix documented drift.

**When decisions do change:** add or update an ADR in `docs/adr/` and update affected sections in the **same change set** as the code (do not rely on chat-only agreement).

## 🛑 Conflict gate (mandatory before implementation)

When the user requests a **new feature**, **behavior change**, or **non-trivial enhancement**:

1. **Read first** — `.cursorrules`, `docs/adr/`, `docs/design-direction.md`, and relevant `src/lib/types.ts` contracts **before** writing or editing application code.
2. **Compare** — the request against those sources and against existing render pipeline, theme schema, and API proxy code.
3. **If anything conflicts** (e.g. contradicts client-side-only rendering, breaks `PosterTheme` schema, bypasses API proxies, or changes export DPI): **pause**, summarize the conflict in plain language (Traditional Chinese for the user), and **ask the user how to proceed** before implementing. Do not silently pick a side.
4. **If sources are missing or ambiguous**: say so briefly and ask for clarification rather than inventing architecture.

## 🎯 Project Overview & Architecture

- **Product**: Browser-based map poster generator inspired by [originalankur/maptoposter](https://github.com/originalankur/maptoposter). Renders entirely client-side; deploys to **Cloudflare Pages**.
- **Stack**: Vite 8 + React 19 + TypeScript 6 + Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn-style UI (`src/components/ui/`) + Canvas 2D at **300 DPI**.
- **Lint / test**: oxlint (`npm run lint`), Vitest (`npm run test`), Playwright e2e (`npm run test:e2e`).
- **Path alias**: `@/` → `src/` (configured in `vite.config.ts`).

### Directory layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/features/editor/` | `EditorApp`, `usePosterGenerator` — orchestration hook |
| `src/features/render/` | Canvas drawing (`drawPoster`), projection, road styles, typography |
| `src/features/osm/` | Overpass query builder, feature parsing, IndexedDB cache |
| `src/features/geocode/` | Nominatim client (via `/api/geocode` proxy) |
| `src/features/themes/` | `themeRegistry` — built-in theme lookup and custom theme merge |
| `src/features/export/` | PNG export, batch ZIP, size presets |
| `src/themes/` | 17 built-in theme JSON files (upstream-ported palette) |
| `src/lib/` | Shared types (`types.ts`), URL/localStorage state (`urlState.ts`), utils |
| `src/components/ui/` | Reusable shadcn-style primitives — extend here, do not duplicate |
| `functions/api/` | Cloudflare Pages Functions — production API proxies |
| `vite.dev-proxy.ts` | Dev-server middleware mirroring `functions/api/` |
| `e2e/` | Playwright specs with mocked `/api/geocode` and `/api/overpass` |

### Feature modules

Keep domain logic in `src/features/<domain>/`. UI composition lives in `EditorApp.tsx` or future feature components — do not put render/OSM/geocode logic inline in JSX.

## 🖼️ Rendering Pipeline Invariants

1. **Client-side only**: All poster drawing happens in the browser via Canvas 2D. No server-side rendering, no Python/matplotlib, no image API round trips for generation.
2. **300 DPI export**: `DPI = 300` in `src/lib/types.ts`. Pixel size = `Math.round(inches × DPI)`. Preview uses a smaller canvas (`previewScale`); export uses full resolution.
3. **Size limits**: `MAX_INCHES = 20`. Clamp width/height via `clampInches()` in `src/features/export/presets.ts`.
4. **Draw order** (do not reorder without visual review): background → gradient fade → water polygons → park polygons → roads (sorted by `roadZIndex`) → typography labels.
5. **Projection**: Lat/lon → canvas via `createProjector` / `fitToCanvas` in `src/features/render/projection.ts`. Viewport is a circle defined by `latitude`, `longitude`, `radiusMeters`.
6. **Road classification**: Colors and widths come from `roadStyle.ts` using `highway` tag → `PosterTheme` road color keys (`road_motorway` … `road_residential`, `road_default` fallback).
7. **OSM layers**: `OsmFeature.layer` is one of `water` | `parks` | `roads`. Overpass query in `overpass.ts` fetches highways, water (ways/relations), waterways, parks, grass, forest within `radiusMeters`.
8. **Fonts**: Load via Google Fonts in `typography.ts` before drawing. `scriptDetection.ts` picks CJK-capable fallbacks when labels contain non-Latin scripts.
9. **Web Worker**: ADR 0001 mentions Workers for off-main-thread rendering; current implementation draws on the main thread. Introduce a Worker only with an ADR update and measurable perf need — do not assume one exists.

## 🎨 Theme System

- **Schema**: `PosterTheme` in `src/lib/types.ts` — `name`, `description`, `bg`, `text`, `gradient_color`, `water`, `parks`, and six `road_*` color keys. All values are CSS hex strings.
- **Built-in themes**: JSON files in `src/themes/`. Register new themes in `themeRegistry.ts` (import + `THEME_REGISTRY` entry). Keep filenames `snake_case.json`.
- **Custom themes**: Runtime override via `PosterConfig.customTheme`; merged over `DEFAULT_THEME` in `loadTheme()`. Theme JSON editor in UI serializes/deserializes this object.
- **Do not** change theme key names without updating `drawPoster.ts`, `roadStyle.ts`, and all JSON theme files in the same change set.

## 🌐 API Proxies (dev + production must stay in sync)

External geocoding and Overpass calls **must** go through app proxies — never call Nominatim or Overpass directly from browser production code (CORS and rate-limit policy).

| Route | Method | Dev | Production |
|-------|--------|-----|------------|
| `/api/geocode` | GET | `vite.dev-proxy.ts` | `functions/api/geocode.ts` |
| `/api/overpass` | POST `{ query }` | `vite.dev-proxy.ts` | `functions/api/overpass.ts` |

**Geocode**: `?city=…&country=…` → Nominatim search (with optional KV edge cache), returns `{ latitude, longitude, displayName }` and `X-Cache: HIT|MISS`. Errors: 400 (missing params), 404 (no results), 502 (upstream failure).

**Overpass**: POST JSON body with `query` string → fan-out to multiple public endpoints (`OVERPASS_ENDPOINTS`), return first success. Errors: 400 (invalid/missing query), 502 (all endpoints failed).

When changing proxy behaviour, update **both** `vite.dev-proxy.ts` and the matching `functions/api/*.ts` file in the same change set. Geocode KV keys must use [`shared/proxyCacheKeys.ts`](shared/proxyCacheKeys.ts). Keep `User-Agent` strings consistent (`mapposter-web/1.0`).

## 💾 State & Persistence

- **Shareable URL**: Hash fragment `#p=<base64 JSON>` via `encodePosterState` / `decodePosterState` in `urlState.ts`. Hash wins over localStorage on load.
- **Autosave**: `localStorage` key `mapposter:autosave` — written on config change and after successful generate.
- **OSM cache**: IndexedDB `mapposter-cache` / store `osm`, keyed by `latitude:longitude:radiusMeters` (5-decimal lat/lon, rounded radius). Cache is per-viewport, not per-theme.
- **Generation phases**: `idle` → `geocoding` → `fetching` → `rendering` → `done` | `error` (also `exporting` during PNG/ZIP). UI reads `GenerationProgress` from `usePosterGenerator`.

## 📤 Export

- **Presets**: `EXPORT_PRESETS` in `src/features/export/presets.ts` — Instagram, mobile/HD/4K wallpaper, A4, default poster (12×16 in). Add presets here; do not hardcode sizes in UI.
- **Single PNG**: `exportPosterPng` — full 300 DPI canvas, downloaded as `{city}_{themeId}.png`.
- **Batch ZIP**: `exportAllThemesZip` — all built-in themes for current viewport/features via JSZip. CPU-heavy; keep progress feedback.
- **Export requires prior generate**: `features` array must be populated; throw clear error if empty.

## 🎨 UI Guidelines

Follow `docs/design-direction.md`:

- **Layout**: Two-column desktop shell — location + style controls (left ~1/2), preview (right ~1/2). Export (size + downloads) lives in a Preview header popover. `max-w-[1600px]` container.
- **Tokens**: shadcn semantic tokens in `src/index.css` (`--background`, `--primary`, etc.). Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid hardcoded hex in editor chrome (poster themes are separate).
- **Components**: Extend `src/components/ui/` (Button, Card, Input, Slider, Tabs, Badge, Spinner, …). Match existing `cva` + `cn()` patterns from `src/lib/utils.ts`.
- **Icons**: `lucide-react`. Use `data-icon="inline-start"` on icons inside buttons (existing convention).
- **Toasts**: `sonner` via `<Toaster richColors position="top-center" />`.
- **Dark mode**: CSS variables support `.dark`, but the app does not expose a theme toggle yet — do not add system dark-mode switching unless requested.
- **Mobile**: Stacked layout is a future enhancement; do not break desktop three-column grid when adding responsive behaviour.

## 🧪 Testing

- **Unit**: Vitest + jsdom. Place tests in `src/test/` or co-located `*.test.ts`. Mock fetch for API modules.
- **E2E**: Playwright in `e2e/`. Mock `/api/geocode` and `/api/overpass` — do not hit real Nominatim/Overpass in CI.
- Run `npm run test` and `npm run test:e2e` after changes to render pipeline, URL state, or API clients.

## 🚀 Deployment (Cloudflare Pages)

- Build: `npm run build` → output `dist/`
- Functions: `functions/` directory (Pages Functions)
- `public/_redirects` for SPA routing if present
- No server secrets required for core poster flow; proxies are stateless

## 🛠️ Code Quality Rules

- **No Code Clipping**: Write out complete file implementations. Do NOT truncate blocks using `// todo` or `// ... rest of code`.
- **TypeScript**: Prefer explicit types from `src/lib/types.ts`. Avoid `any`; use narrow types for OSM tags and API payloads.
- **Imports**: Use `@/` alias. Group: external → `@/components` → `@/features` → `@/lib` → relative.
- **New dependencies**: Justify additions. Prefer existing stack (idb, jszip, radix, tailwind) over new libraries.
- **Minimize scope**: Match surrounding code style. Reuse `usePosterGenerator`, `drawPoster`, and existing UI primitives rather than parallel implementations.
